      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;">In the past quarter, the **Campus‑to‑Home Route** has set new benchmarks for reliability and transparency, turning everyday commutes into a model of operational excellence. Our average transit time for the 12‑mile stretch now sits at just **45 minutes**, a 12 % reduction from the previous cycle, thanks to optimized routing and dedicated driver training. This speed gain is matched by a stellar on‑time delivery rate of **98 %**, meaning that the vast majority of students and staff arrive exactly when they expect, without the late‑night anxieties that once plagued campus‑to‑home trips.

Central to this success is our real‑time GPS update system. Every vehicle broadcasts its position every 10 seconds, allowing the dispatch center to track progress, anticipate delays, and provide passengers with accurate arrival estimates directly on their smartphones. The live feed also powers our dynamic “checkpoint advisories” – automated notifications that surface when a bus is approaching a key intersection, such as the busy “Main St. / Maple Ave.” junction, or when weather conditions might affect traffic flow. These alerts give riders peace of mind and a clear sense of when to expect their pickup or drop‑off.

The checkpoint advisories themselves are more than just warnings; they are proactive tools that help the route maintain its high on‑time rate. By flagging potential bottlenecks 15 minutes ahead, drivers can adjust their speed or take alternate lanes, preventing the ripple effects of a single delay. The system also integrates with campus security to ensure that any incidents—whether a stalled vehicle or an unexpected road closure—are communicated instantly to all stakeholders.

Collectively, these performance highlights demonstrate that the **Campus‑to‑Home Route** is not merely a transportation corridor but a data‑driven, rider‑centric experience. Students can now rely on a dependable schedule, real‑time visibility, and timely advisories that keep them informed every step of the way. As we look ahead, the goal is to push the average transit time even lower while sustaining the 98 % on‑time delivery rate, all powered by the same robust GPS and advisory framework that has already earned the trust of our campus community.</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>



